0..75 Comment "//! The two searches of `boot-core` over `Ptr.Eff`: the first position of a"
76..142 Comment "//! byte in a range, and the first position of a range in a range."
143..146 Comment "//!"
147..221 Comment "//! `find_byte` and `find_range` give the answers of the Rust functions of"
222..299 Comment "//! `crates/boot-core/src/search.rs`. They name no model of memory: the scope"
300..374 Comment "//! that handles `Ptr.Eff` chooses one. Each reads one byte at a time with"
375..452 Comment "//! `load8`, and it reads no byte outside its ranges. An empty range can have"
453..493 Comment "//! any address, and no search reads it."
494..497 Comment "//!"
498..575 Comment "//! The length of a range counts its bytes one step at a time, so each search"
576..650 Comment "//! descends on a length. A loop that counts down a word holds its counter"
651..713 Comment "//! across a load, which a handler may resume other than once."
714..717 Comment "//!"
718..796 Comment "//! The `runs` items run the cases of `crates/boot-core/tests/search.rs` under"
797..875 Comment "//! `Extent`. Each range ends at the end of the extent, so a read past it ends"
876..948 Comment "//! the run with `Outside`, as a read past a page with no access faults."
949..952 Comment "//!"
953..1027 Comment "//! - see: `../../../library/std/src/ptr.gandr` — `Ptr.Eff` and `Extent`"
1028..1103 Comment "//! - see: `../../../crates/boot-core/src/search.rs` — the Rust functions"
